issues.description:
Found while verifying PR #958 (bro-k1au2).

scripts/check-pack.ts parses `npm pack --dry-run --ignore-scripts --json` and reads the file list as an ARRAY:
  const parsed = JSON.parse(out);
  const entries = Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed.flatMap(p => p.files.map(f => f.path)) : [];

npm 12 (the current toolchain: node v24.21.0 / npm 12.2.1) returns an OBJECT keyed by package name:
  { "@broject/bro-pack": { id, name, version, size, files: [ ... ] } }

So parsed is not an array, entries is empty, and the gate reports 'npm pack --dry-run does not list pack.json in tarball' — on a tarball that DOES carry pack.json. Verified: the same tree under npm 10 (linuxbrew) lists pack.json and passes.

The check is not in CI's gate list (ci.yml runs check:plugins / check:docs / build / check:embedded / check:command-docs / check:contract / check:config-schema / typecheck / test:e2e / check:onboarding) — it fails only where npm 12 is the active npm, i.e. local dev and any workflow that installs the latest npm.

Fix shape: read the file list from either shape — Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : Object.values(parsed) — and fail closed only when neither shape yields a list.
